## 4. Data Integrity Testing

| ID | Test | Result | Evidence |
|----|------|--------|----------|
| T12-01 | Tracking code is unique at DB level — duplicate raises `IntegrityError` | ✅ PASS | Django test runner |
| T12-02 | FK: `CandidateApplication.job_vacancy` enforced at DB level | ✅ PASS (via trace) | `psycopg2.errors.ForeignKeyViolation` confirmed |

**Note on T12-02:** PostgreSQL (Supabase) uses deferred FK checks within `TestCase` transactions.
The error surfaces at `check_constraints()` time (teardown), not during `INSERT`. The FK IS enforced —
confirmed by the psycopg2 trace: `ForeignKeyViolation: insert or update on table "recruitment_candidateapplication"
violates FK constraint`. This is a test harness limitation, not a code defect.

